# Payments platform review

kpi Uptime | 99.97% | +0.02 pts | good
kpi p99 latency | 182 ms | -12% | good
kpi Monthly cost | $41,200 | +8% | bad
kpi Incidents | 3 | | down from 5

## Architecture

diagram aws dir=LR title="Production topology"
aws: user "Customer" user
aws: cf "CloudFront" ext
aws: alb "Public ALB" lb
aws: api "Payments API" svc "ECS · 6 tasks" focus
aws: worker "Settlement worker" fn
aws: q "settlement-q" queue
aws: db "Orders DB" db "Aurora PG 16"
aws: stripe "Stripe" ext
aws: group pub "Public subnets" alb
aws: group priv "Private subnets" api, worker, q, db
aws: group vpc "VPC 10.20.0.0/16" pub, priv
aws: group prod "Prod account 4411" vpc
aws: user -> cf -> alb : https
aws: alb -> api
aws: api -> db : sql
aws: api -> q : enqueue
aws: q --> worker : poll
aws: worker -> stripe : payout
aws: stripe --> api : webhook

## Login flow

diagram login sequence title="OAuth login with PKCE"
login: browser "Browser" user
login: app "Web app" svc
login: idp "Identity provider" ext
login: browser -> app : GET /login
login: app --> browser : 302 to IdP
login: browser -> idp : authorize + code_challenge
login: note idp : user signs in with MFA
login: idp --> browser : code
login: browser -> app : code
login: app -> idp : token + code_verifier
login: idp --> app : id_token
login: app -> app : create session

